  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "A triangle and a trapezoid are equal in area. They also have the same altitude. If the base of the triangle is \\(18\\) inches, the median of the trapezoid is:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(36\\) inches"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(9\\) inches"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(18\\) inches"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "not obtainable from these data"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "none of these"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "b",
    "value": "9"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1953-p13.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "If the common altitude is \\(h,\\) the triangle has area \\[ \\frac12(18)h=9h. \\] A trapezoid’s area is its median times its altitude, so its median must be \\(9\\) inches.\n\nThus, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "The area of a trapezoid is its median times its altitude",
        "Compare \\(mh\\) with \\(\\tfrac12(18)h\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
